SYNTHESIS
========================================================================
1. The permutohedron lift is the right geometry: each row is a
   one-parameter path through adjacent-swap chambers, and the LRC
   target is exactly the long-long facet at the observer.
2. The tempting raw lemma 'every blocker-owner handoff crosses source'
   is false in the hard rows: raw_handoff_defects are nonzero and
   blocker owner states can have nontrivial SCCs.  So the free graph
   obstruction from HYP-1997 survives in permutohedral language.
3. The useful refinement is labelled debt: hard handoffs that avoid
   source are precisely where endpoint debt is exported to deeper
   quotient layers (seven-ladder -> gate-ladder -> double-gate).
4. A plausible n=14 proof should combine this chamber ledger with a
   Farkas/Hall endpoint-debt certificate: no closed blocker-owner
   circulation in the permutohedral fan should be realizable after all
   private endpoint leaves are peeled.
5. This session therefore does not prove n=14.  It narrows the proof
   target to a labelled permutohedral handoff theorem, rather than a
   scalar gap argument or a pure metagraph feedback-vertex argument.
